rem signed-slice `index` sign-extension fixture (i8/i16/i32/i64) — a negative
rem element must come back NEGATIVE on BOTH backends. A both-agree-wrong bug was
rem here: `index` read the raw bytes UNSIGNED, so slice i32 of -1 → 4294967295.
rem The element's TYPE is signed, so index must sign-extend. Unsigned stays unsigned.
module m .

fn s8  input s slice i8  . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .
fn s16 input s slice i16 . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .
fn s32 input s slice i32 . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .
fn s64 input s slice i64 . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .

rem positive control — a small positive signed element stays positive.
fn s32p input s slice i32 . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .

rem unsigned control — index of 0xFFFFFFFF stays 4294967295, NOT -1.
fn u32 input s slice u32 . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx s. 0 . . . end .

rem view_array route — a signed typed view must sign-extend too.
def type bytes slice u8 .
fn v32 input b bytes . output i64 . do return widen i64 idx view_array i32 b. . 0 . . . end .
